    "organization": null,
    "title": "Thunderbolt Core",
    "description": "The required core library for AE2 Lightning Tech, providing AE2LT with autocrafting optimizations, overloaded channels, and low-level infrastructure.",
    "body": "# Thunderbolt Core\n\nThunderbolt Core is a required core dependency developed primarily for AE2 Lightning Tech (AE2LT). It provides AE2LT with autocrafting optimizations, overloaded-channel support, matrix-crafting infrastructure, and other low-level features.\n\nIf you are installing AE2 Lightning Tech, you must also install Thunderbolt Core.\n\nThunderbolt Core can also be installed independently alongside Applied Energistics 2 to improve AE2 autocrafting planning and task dispatch. However, standalone use is secondary—the main purpose of this mod is to provide the core functionality required by AE2 Lightning Tech.\n\n## Features\n\n- Required core infrastructure for AE2 Lightning Tech\n- Overloaded-channel infrastructure for AE2LT\n- Matrix-crafting infrastructure for AE2LT\n- Faster AE2 autocrafting planning\n- Efficient batch dispatch for crafting tasks\n- Crafting extension APIs for compatible addons\n- Optional compatibility hooks for Advanced AE, NeoECO, AE2 Crafting Tree, and ExtendedAE Plus\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Minecraft 1.21.1\n- NeoForge 21.1.x\n- Applied Energistics 2 19.2.17–19.2.x\n\nThunderbolt Core and AE2 must be installed on both the client and the server.\n\nThunderbolt Core is required when using AE2 Lightning Tech. It may also be installed without AE2LT, but only its standalone AE2 optimization and infrastructure features will be available.\n\n## Issues and Feedback\n\nIf you encounter a compatibility problem, crash, or unexpected autocrafting behavior, please report it through GitHub Issues:\n\nhttps://github.com/ae2lt/Thunderbolt-Core/issues\n\nPlease include your logs, mod list, and reproduction steps whenever possible.\n\n## License\n\nThunderbolt Core is licensed under the GNU LGPL 3.0.",
